# Build-context whitelist for the relay image (build context = repo root,
# see relay/Dockerfile). Everything not listed below stays out of the image
# build context — keeps builds fast and guarantees zero secrets/keys shipped.
*
!relay/app/
!relay/requirements.txt
!relay/Dockerfile
!relay/registrar.py
!contracts/out/Escrow.sol/Escrow.json
!contracts/out/Registry.sol/Registry.json
# re-excluded after the directory re-include (order matters in dockerignore)
relay/app/**/__pycache__/

# --- Defense in depth (the `*` whitelist above already excludes everything
# else; these explicit re-exclusions are belt-and-braces so a later accidental
# `!` re-include can never leak runtime/secret material, including nested
# copies of app-data dirs) ---
# env files at ANY depth (`.env.example` is not in the allowlist either).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# keystore material and its atomic-write temp copies (app/keystore.py writes
# .keystore-*.tmp next to the target before os.replace) — even inside the
# allowed app/ tree.
**/keystore.json
**/keystore.json.*
**/.keystore-*
**/appdata/
**/tmp/
**/secrets/
relay/data/
